      "lyrics": {
        "pd": {
          "lyricist": "Traditional",
          "basis": "traditional",
          "detail": "Anonymous American work-ballad text with no identifiable author, sung in southern railroad and steel-driving camps from the 1870s and collected from oral tradition long before any of it reached print.",
          "sourceEdition": "Sandburg, 'The American Songbag', Harcourt, Brace & Company, 1927, pp. 24-25 ('John Henry'; the twelve stanzas are printed on p. 25), stanzas 1, 3 and 6"
        },
        "notes": "Three of Sandburg's twelve stanzas, transcribed from the 1927 printing and nowhere else; no modern revival wording is carried. Sandburg's stanza 4 carries a racial slur in its second line, addressed to the shaker, and the whole stanza is omitted rather than reworded. The remaining stanzas are dropped for length only. Sandburg's transcribed eye-dialect spelling is set in standard orthography here - the words and the sung syllables are his, only the spelling is normalised, so the chart stays readable. Each stanza is four sung lines over four four-bar phrases, so they fall on bars 0, 4, 8 and 12; Sandburg prints a fifth line that simply repeats the fourth, and the tune here has no phrase for it. Line 1's pickup is carried at the end of the intro, and the low 5 at beat 63 is the pickup into the next verse.",
        "stanzas": [
          [
            { "bar": 0, "text": "John Henry told his captain" },
            { "bar": 4, "text": "That a man was a natural man" },
            { "bar": 8, "text": "And before he'd let that steam drill run him down" },
            { "bar": 12, "text": "He'd fall dead with a hammer in his hand" }
          ],
          [
            { "bar": 0, "text": "John Henry says to his captain" },
            { "bar": 4, "text": "Send me a twelve-pound hammer around" },
            { "bar": 8, "text": "A twelve-pound hammer with a four-foot handle" },
            { "bar": 12, "text": "And I beat your steam drill down" }
          ],
          [
            { "bar": 0, "text": "John Henry hammered in the mountains" },
            { "bar": 4, "text": "The mountains was so high" },
            { "bar": 8, "text": "The last words I heard the poor boy say" },
            { "bar": 12, "text": "Give me a cool drink of water 'fore I die" }
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
